[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two simple, wide-rimmed matte ceramic bowls positioned on an aged, weathered oak kitchen table. The bowls are placed side-by-side at a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring every component is clearly visible. The foreground bowl is sharp with a shallow depth of field, while the second bowl rests slightly behind in soft focus. Soft natural light streams from a window on the left, casting gentle, diffused shadows across the table. Inside the bowls, a bed of vibrant, mixed baby greens provides a fresh base. A colorful mixture of nutty brown rice, crisp red apple chunks, and bright green sliced celery is spooned over the greens. Generous, rustic flakes of pink salmon sit prominently atop the mixture, showing natural, tender textures. The dish is finished with a scattering of crunchy chopped walnuts. A light, glistening apple cider and Dijon vinaigrette coats the ingredients, providing a subtle, realistic sheen. Props include a wooden spoon resting casually on the table near the bowls, and a few stray walnut fragments and a single slice of apple scattered on the wood surface, appearing as if just prepared. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, and authentic. Includes slight natural imperfections like an asymmetric scatter of walnuts and a tiny drip of vinaigrette on the bowl rim. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial cookbook photography."
]
